    "probe_text": "The endpoint `POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (the V2 controller only exposes a paged list). Here is everything applied, in execution order.\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Request-level Bean Validation** \u2014 the parameter is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnersApi.java:86`), so the DTO constraints fire before `addOwner` executes:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(3..255)`, `@Email` (only when present)\n\n## Inside `addOwner` (top to bottom)\n\n3. **`rejectMissingOrBlankFields`** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects if `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, or `telephone` is null/blank, or if `address` is blank *after normalization*. Throws `RequiredFieldsMissingException`. (Note: address blankness is checked here via `normalizeAddress`, but the normalized value is not yet stored.)\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.\n5. **`normalizeAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 strip/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; result stored on the owner.\n6. **`normalizeTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 strip spaces/dashes/brackets, convert to E.164 (assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` when no `+`); must be `+` then 8\u201315 digits, with `+61`\u2192exactly 9 national digits and `+1`\u2192exactly 10. Throws `InvalidTelephoneException`. Normalized value stored.\n7. **`normalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 null passes through; otherwise trim, syntactic check against `EMAIL_PATTERN` (throws `InvalidEmailException`), lower-case, then reject disposable domains `mailinator.com`/`tempmail.com`/`guerrillamail.com` (throws `DisposableEmailDomainException`). Normalized value stored.\n8. **`validatePostcode`** *(validation)* \u2014 null passes; else must be 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region \u2192 any 4-digit ok). Throws `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n9. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** *(validation)* \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today, throw `FutureRegistrationDateException` (checked against the *supplied* value, before any adjustment).\n10. **Default registration date** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if null, set to `LocalDate.now()`.\n11. **`rollToBusinessDay`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if Saturday roll to Monday (+2), if Sunday roll to Monday (+1); weekday unchanged. Stored as the owner's `registrationDate`.\n12. **`rejectDailyLimitReached`** *(validation)* \u2014 reject if \u2265 100 existing owners already share that (adjusted) `registrationDate`. Throws `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n13. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** *(validation)* \u2014 reject if \u2265 50 existing owners already share the city (case-insensitive). Throws `CityOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n14. **`computeHouseholdId`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 set `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`.\n15. **Read `sharesHousehold`** \u2014 from the DTO (`true`/`false`).\n16. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** *(validation)* \u2014 reject if any existing owner has the same `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`). Throws `DuplicateIdentityException`. Runs regardless of `sharesHousehold`.\n17. **`rejectHouseholdDuplicate`** *(validation, conditional)* \u2014 only when `sharesHousehold` is not true: reject if any existing owner already shares the `householdId`. Throws `HouseholdDuplicateException`.\n18. **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` and only if postcode present, set `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` to the lowest-id existing owner sharing last name + postcode but with a different telephone.\n19. **`generateCustomerCode`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 set `customerCode` = `<region>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 of `telephone + lastName`).\n20. **`countNamesakes`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 set `namesakeCount` = existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new one.\n21. **`countHouseholdSize`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 set `householdSize` = existing owners sharing `householdId`, plus 1.\n22. **`isBulkSignupDay`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 set `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 existing owners already share the `registrationDate`.\n23. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** *(side-effect: persist)* \u2014 persists the owner. At flush, the JPA/Hibernate entity constraints on `Owner` also apply: `@NotEmpty` on `address`, `city`, `telephone`, and `@Pattern ^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` on `telephone`.\n24. **Audit log** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...\")`.\n25. **`Location` header** *(side-effect)* \u2014 set to `/api/owners/{id}`; respond `201 CREATED` with the mapped `OwnerDto`.\n\nA few things worth flagging: the blank-field, telephone, email, and postcode checks run against the *normalized* values; `registrationDate`'s business-day adjustment happens **before** the daily-limit count, so the limit is measured against the rolled date; and `rejectDuplicateIdentity` always runs while `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` is skipped when `sharesHousehold=true`."
